        "original_id": "ff2ae548-0ae4-56a4-9e41-54412e8bccbc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frank Wentz, John Christy, Roy Spencer\n- Organizations: University of Alabama in Huntsville, NASA\n- Systems: UAH satellite temperature record, RSS satellite temperature record, Advanced Microwave Scanning Radiometer (AMSR-E), Aqua satellite\n- Roles: meteorologist, principal research scientist, U.S. Science Team leader\n\nFacts:\n- Roy Warren Spencer was born on December 20, 1955.\n- Roy Spencer is a meteorologist and a principal research scientist at the University of Alabama in Huntsville.\n- Roy Spencer is the U.S. Science Team leader for the Advanced Microwave Scanning Radiometer (AMSR-E) on NASA's Aqua satellite.\n- John Christy and Roy Spencer developed the earlier UAH satellite temperature record.\n- Intercomparison with the earlier UAH satellite temperature record revealed deficiencies in that earlier work.\n- The RSS satellite temperature record shows a larger warming trend than the University of Alabama in Huntsville (UAH) record.",
